# The `caos-build` tool (SPEC, "Tools"): the dev/test-stack worker image with
# this directory's script curried onto it, plus the `help` an agent registers
# it by. It moved out of caos-tools/ into std/ so the agent harness can DEPend on
# it and register it ALWAYS — the tool comes from the harness's own version, not
# from whatever tree is being worked on (design/flake-inputs.md, "the tui").
#
# dev/test-stack, not std/bash: this tool needs nix and a persistent store, and
# those are grants only an image can declare in its own config.
#
# The docs are a HERE-STRING, so they live here rather than in the script — and
# a `.caos-expr` is STRIPPED from the tree it is evaluated against, so editing
# them re-keys this tool's arg tree and nothing it builds.
HELP=<<END
Compile the caos tree with `nix build`, in a container that has the host's nix
store persisted in a volume — so an unchanged dependency is a lookup rather than
a rebuild. Returns the build log, ending in OK or FAILED. A failed build is a
result to read, not an error that ends the turn. This tool is specific to the
caos codebase; run in any other tree it reports cleanly that there is nothing
for it to build.
END
curry --base:@=DEEP-DEPS/test-stack --worker1:@=worker.sh --help=$HELP
